{
  "baseline_label": "proxy-ac-eager",
  "baseline_tokens_per_second": 8591.691840286141,
  "boundary": "RTX 3090 sm_86 measurements in synthetic compute mode with accumulation chosen for local tractability. Relative ordering is evidence for configuration selection; absolute throughput and the microbatch and checkpointing decisions must be remeasured on GH200. FLA autotune configurations are Hopper-tuned, so kernel rankings may differ there. No GPU-hours from the grant allocation were consumed and no data or model was admitted.",
  "date": "2026-09-21",
  "engineering_only": true,
  "findings": {
    "compile_requires_checkpointing_off": "With activation checkpointing enabled, torch.compile returns 1.008x because the @torch.compiler.disable on FLA chunk_kda breaks Dynamo's speculate_subgraph and each checkpointed block falls back to eager. With it disabled, compile returns 1.612x.",
    "determinism_cost": "1.098x at default compile and 1.086x at max-autotune. Raising the microbatch to two recovers more than determinism costs, so determinism can be retained.",
    "flagship_activation_checkpointing_off": "Does not fit a 24 GiB card. Two attempts reached 23.03 and 22.91 GiB allocated before out-of-memory, so the flagship checkpointing decision must be measured on GH200.",
    "in_kernel_gate": "FLA use_gate_in_kernel is a memory optimization, not a speed one: no measurable throughput change, 1.14 GiB less backward peak at microbatch two. Outputs and gradients agree with the precomputed gate to 7.4e-4 relative, which is bfloat16 level.",
    "remaining_bottleneck": "At the best configuration GEMM and mixer kernels are 69.3% of device time. The largest remaining single item is Command Buffer Full at 9.9%, which is launch pressure from the six graph breaks. CUDA graphs are unavailable until those breaks are removed."
  },
